    thinking: "**Defining App Features**\n\nI\'m currently outlining the core features and UI screens required for **MY LIBRARY** app using Kotlin Jetpack Compose. This includes thinking through the GitHub repo structure, SQL migrations, seed data, and edge cases. I\'m focusing on defining the scope for the mobile application build, and making some notes about how these elements will work together!\n\n\n**Planning Data Models**\n\nI\'ve been working on the data models for the native Android app, specifically the `app/src/main/java/com/example/...` directory. I\'m focusing on the integration with Supabase, including configuring the URL and Anon Key. I\'ve defined the structure for essential models such as `OwnerProfile`, `Library`, `Branch`, `Floor`, `Room`, `Seat`, `Shift`, and `Student`. These models will incorporate fields and their relationships.\n\n\n**Defining Data Tables**\n\nI\'m now outlining database tables for the application. Key tables include `Student`, `LibraryPlan`, `StudentSubscription`, `StudentPayment`, `Expense`, `AttendanceRecord`, and `SaaSSubscription`. Each table has specific fields like IDs, names, dates, amounts, and statuses, with appropriate data types. I\'m focusing on ensuring data integrity and optimizing for efficient queries within the Supabase setup. I\'m also considering how relationships between these tables will be defined.\n\n\n**Designing Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now expanding the database design with crucial tables such as `AuditLog`, `RegistrationRequest`, and `SupportTicket`, along with their respective fields and data types. These new tables will facilitate better tracking, user registration, and support functionality within the application. I am thinking about how to effectively manage these new data structures within the Supabase framework.\n\n**Structuring Data Access**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the data access layer. I\'m building a `SupabaseApiClient` to interact with Supabase REST API endpoints using the proper headers. A local, reactive state cache, compatible with Room, will ensure smooth operation even with slow networks. I am planning the implementation of a `LibraryViewModel` which will manage authentication, onboarding, and dashboard states to improve user experience.\n\n\n**Outlining Core Features**\n\nI\'m now detailing user operations, focusing on student, attendance, and fee management. I\'m also planning the interactive seat map and shift management features. I\'m now thinking through a SaaS subscription upgrade modal and registration requests review, alongside filterable report exports with relevant upgrade restrictions. Finally, I\'m integrating a QR code generator for self-registration.\n\n\n**Defining UI Style**\n\nI am now focusing on the app\'s visual design. I\'m aiming for a modern look using a color palette of Royal Navy, Slate, Electric Teal, Golden Amber, Emerald Green, and Rose Red. I want to use crisp white cards with rounded corners, modern typography, and elevation. I\'m exploring the design of the authentication screen and the onboarding wizard, which will consist of eight steps. The main screen will have bottom navigation with a dashboard, and I\'m currently defining these key screens.\n\n\n**Designing Dashboard Layout**\n\nI am now structuring the dashboard screen, which will include key performance indicator cards such as revenue, active students, and seat occupancy. I plan to incorporate quick action cards for student, attendance, and expense management, as well as action-required alerts for expiring dues and pending approvals. Recent student activity and live stream elements are also being planned. I\'m focusing on user interface design for the students and the seat tabs.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 113059230
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
