    thinking: "**Investigating Clickability Issues**\n\nI\'m currently looking into the clickability problem on the home page. My focus is on the `DashboardScreen.kt` and `MainActivity.kt` files. I\'m checking the quick action cards in `DashboardScreen`, specifically the \"+ Student\" option, to see what actions are triggered. I am trying to determine if there\'s an issue with the navigation or dialog opening.\n\n\n**Analyzing Navigation Parameters**\n\nI\'ve been re-examining the `DashboardScreen.kt` file. It appears the issue isn\'t with clickability per se, but with the lack of navigation parameters. Specifically, the quick action for \"Expenses\" isn\'t set up to navigate, unlike others such as \"Attendance\" or \"Reports\". It looks like `onNavigateToExpenses` or similar isn\'t even passed into the `DashboardScreen` from `MainActivity`, which is a key observation. The current setup opens dialogs in some quick actions (e.g. \"+ Student\", \"Collect Fee\") rather than navigating, which may be expected behavior; I have to keep that in mind.\n\n\n**Refining Navigation & UX**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user experience improvements. First, the goal is to ensure all click interactions work, and that navigation is explicit. I\'m adding direct navigation to the \"Students\" list and \"Expenses\" tabs, where clicking \"+ Student\" should also open a dialog AND have an option to navigate to the Students list. Also, I have to ensure all dialogs and navigation handlers are correctly connected. I\'m also planning to refine the attendance screen, which is another area of concern.\n\n\n"
