    thinking: "**Examining MainActivity.kt**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how `MainActivity.kt` handles different screens based on the `selectedTab` state. I\'m digging into how dialogs triggered by the `viewModel`, like `_showAddStudentDialog`, are managed within this context. The goal is to fully understand the flow and coordination of screen transitions and dialog presentations.\n\n\n**Analyzing DashboardScreen.kt**\n\nI\'ve moved on to examining `DashboardScreen.kt`, specifically focusing on the non-clickable actions within the quick access and actions sections on the home page. The user\'s input highlighted issues with \"+ Student,\" \"+ Expense,\" and other actions, as they don\'t trigger the expected dialogs. I\'m exploring how navigation and event handling are implemented within this screen, considering how to correctly connect the quick actions to the appropriate dialog presentations and navigation targets.\n\n\n**Refining Quick Action Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the quick action logic within `DashboardScreen.kt`. Specifically, I\'m defining the actions within the quick access section. I\'m focusing on the click behaviors and the associated event handling for \"Students\" and \"+ Student,\" \"Attendance,\" \"Collect Fee,\" \"Seat Map,\" \"Expenses,\" \"+ Add Expense,\" \"Reports,\" \"Public QR,\" and \"All Present\" actions. The intention is to define whether clicks navigate or open a dialog.\n\n\n**Centralizing Dialog Rendering**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the centralization of dialog rendering. My current focus is to ensure all dialogs triggered by `LibraryViewModel`, such as the add student or add expense dialogs, are rendered in `MainActivity.kt` (or globally). The aim is to guarantee a smooth and consistent dialog appearance across the app, regardless of the active screen.\nI am also exploring how to navigate to specific screens when certain KPI cards or Quick Actions are clicked on the dashboard. I\'m noting that clicking \"Active Students\" should go to the students screen.\n\n\n**Updating AttendanceScreen.kt**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI updates for `AttendanceScreen.kt`. I\'ve removed the \"Late\" and \"Leave\" buttons, leaving only \"Present\" and \"Absent.\" I\'m updating the status summary pills to reflect these changes, including \"Present,\" \"Absent,\" and \"Total Active\" student counts. Furthermore, I\'m integrating a date selector banner, enabling navigation between dates and a date picker, which will be accessible via a calendar button.\n\n\n**Implementing Attendance Editability**\n\nI am now focusing on implementing the attendance editability rules. My current approach involves calculating the difference between the selected date and today to determine if attendance records are editable. I\'ve defined rules for different date ranges: today, yesterday, and the day before yesterday are editable, while older dates become read-only. I\'m also addressing the handling of future dates, which will remain locked. I need to ensure a clear display of the current edit status via badges such as \"Today \342\200\242 Editable\" and banners for locked dates such as \"\360\237\224\222 Historical Record (Older Than 2 Days)\" and provide the corresponding logic.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 673098985
    }
