  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Centralizing Dialog Handling**\n\nI\'m currently focused on centralizing the dialog management within `MainActivity.kt`. My aim is to have this class handle all dialog interactions, including `AddStudentDialog`, `CollectFeeDialog`, `AddExpenseDialog`, `ReceiptDialog`, `StudentDetailDialog`, `SeatActionDialog`, `QrPosterDialog`, and `Branch` dialogs. This could improve consistency and make the overall architecture cleaner.\n\n\n**Refining Dialog Interactions**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on how dialogs will behave across different screens. My approach is to make *any* click action, regardless of the screen, immediately trigger the dialog. Whether it\'s the quick action buttons or row items, the expected outcome remains the same: a dialog instantly opens. I\'m also addressing a user feedback point on the home page, specifically the non-clickability of Quick Actions for students and expenses. I must make it clickable!\n\n\n**Defining Quick Actions**\n\nI\'m presently focused on the Quick Actions component on the home screen. I\'m aiming for eight clearly defined and spaced actions: \"Students,\" \"+ Student,\" \"Attendance,\" \"Collect Fee,\" \"Seat Map,\" \"Expenses,\" and \"+ Expense\". Each action will have a corresponding icon and functionality, and I\'m ensuring consistency with existing navigation and dialog interactions.\n\n\n**Expanding Quick Actions**\n\nI\'ve expanded the Quick Actions on the home screen further. I\'ve integrated \"Reports,\" \"Public QR,\" and \"All Present\" with corresponding icons. This ensures all relevant actions are readily accessible and user-friendly.\n\nI\'ve made the \"Expenses\" metric pill in the Hero Banner, and the KPI cards for \"Active Students,\" \"Fee Dues,\" \"Seats Occupancy,\" and \"Present Today\" all clickable. This gives the user more direct access to their most-used functions.\n\nFinally, I am ready to begin revising the attendance flow based on specific user feedback: removing the options for late and leave, and integrating a date picker for flexibility.\n\n\n**Implementing Attendance Updates**\n\nI\'m now revising the attendance flow based on this feedback. I\'ll remove \"Late\" and \"Leave\" options, leaving only \"Present\" and \"Absent\" when the date is editable. I\'m introducing a Date Bar with navigation (`<`, `>`) and a date selector, as well as quick chips for common date selections. I want to make sure past days are not editable once marked, and that we can pick any date in history to check attendance.\n\n\n**Defining Editability Rules**\n\nI am now focusing on editability based on the date. I will show the \'unmarked/present/absent\' toggle if the date is editable (today, yesterday, or the day before). If the date is locked (3+ days ago or future date), I\'ll indicate \"Absent\" or \"Not Marked\". I am keeping track of the diff between the selected date and the current date, to determine the editability. I also added a green badge to indicate dates within the grace period.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 635007624
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
