    thinking: "**Refining Attendance View**\n\nI\'m simplifying the `AttendanceScreen.kt` by focusing on just \"Present\" and \"Absent\" statuses. Also, I\'m integrating date selection using `selectedDateIso` bound to the `viewModel.selectedAttendanceDate.collectAsState()`, and I need to figure out how to display the selected date in an understandable format.\n\n\n**Calculating Date Displays**\n\nI\'ve nailed down the date display logic! I\'m calculating how many days ago a selected date is using `viewModel.getAttendanceDaysAgo()`. Based on this, I\'ll show a friendly badge like \"Today (Editable)\", \"2 Days Ago (Editable)\", or \"Future Date (Locked)\". The editability relies on this calculation and will be shown in the badge too! I\'ve also planned the navigation buttons and the date picker interaction. I\'m excited about the quick chips for rapid date selection.\n\n\n**Defining Editability Logic**\n\nNow I\'m diving into the editability states. When a date is editable, I\'ll provide an \"All Present\" button and interactive Present/Absent buttons for each student. When locked, I\'ll show a lock banner with non-interactive, clear pills and a lock icon in each student card. I\'ll need to figure out how to disable the existing buttons with a locked notice. I\'m starting to visualize this in my mind\'s eye!\n\n\n"
