  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the implementation of the **WhatsApp Fee Due Reminder** feature, seamlessly integrated with your multi-tier subscription plans (gated to the 2nd and 3rd plans \342\200\224 Premium and Business) and designed for high usability and clarity:\n\n### 1. **WhatsApp Fee Due Reminders (2nd & 3rd Plan Feature)**\n- **Owner WhatsApp Due Digest**: When student fees are due, the library owner receives an automated, comprehensive WhatsApp alert listing all students with pending fees, assigned seat numbers, shifts, due dates, and total pending amounts.\n- **Direct Student WhatsApp Reminders**: Send personalized, 1-tap WhatsApp fee payment reminders directly to each student with their pass code, monthly fee breakdown, due date, and library payment details.\n- **SaaS Subscription Gating**: Securely restricted to **Plan 2 (Premium)** and **Plan 3 (Business)** with built-in upgrade prompts for Free Plan users.\n\n### 2. **UI & Workflow Touchpoints**\n- **Dashboard Action Banner**: Highlights pending student dues with a 1-tap *\"Notify Owner on WhatsApp\"* button and quick link to the WhatsApp Reminders Hub.\n- **Student Cards & Profile Dialog**: Quick-action WhatsApp button appears on student cards with dues, allowing instant fee alert dispatching.\n- **WhatsApp Notification Hub**: Complete management dialog with live message preview (Monospace WhatsApp layout) for both owner digest and student reminders.\n- **Operations & Settings**: WhatsApp Fee Due configuration and status visible in the Operations menu.\n\n### 3. **Form Text Visibility & High Contrast**\n- All form inputs across Registration, Student Enrollment, and Fee Collection feature dark, high-contrast text (`#1E293B`) on solid surfaces with distinct focus highlights for clear legibility."
    thinking: "**Verifying Project Completion**\n\nI\'ve got good news! The build is complete. Now, my focus shifts to meticulously checking every element. The first area I\'m scrutinizing is the \"WhatsApp Fee Due Reminder\" notifications. Specifically, I\'m verifying the gating to the Premium and Business plans and confirming their instant delivery.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the implementation of the **WhatsApp Fee Due Reminder** feature, seamlessly integrated with your multi-tier subscription plans (gated to the 2nd and 3rd plans \342\200\224 Premium and Business) and designed for high usability and clarity:\n\n### 1. **WhatsApp Fee Due Reminders (2nd & 3rd Plan Feature)**\n- **Owner WhatsApp Due Digest**: When student fees are due, the library owner receives an automated, comprehensive WhatsApp alert listing all students with pending fees, assigned seat numbers, shifts, due dates, and total pending amounts.\n- **Direct Student WhatsApp Reminders**: Send personalized, 1-tap WhatsApp fee payment reminders directly to each student with their pass code, monthly fee breakdown, due date, and library payment details.\n- **SaaS Subscription Gating**: Securely restricted to **Plan 2 (Premium)** and **Plan 3 (Business)** with built-in upgrade prompts for Free Plan users.\n\n### 2. **UI & Workflow Touchpoints**\n- **Dashboard Action Banner**: Highlights pending student dues with a 1-tap *\"Notify Owner on WhatsApp\"* button and quick link to the WhatsApp Reminders Hub.\n- **Student Cards & Profile Dialog**: Quick-action WhatsApp button appears on student cards with dues, allowing instant fee alert dispatching.\n- **WhatsApp Notification Hub**: Complete management dialog with live message preview (Monospace WhatsApp layout) for both owner digest and student reminders.\n- **Operations & Settings**: WhatsApp Fee Due configuration and status visible in the Operations menu.\n\n### 3. **Form Text Visibility & High Contrast**\n- All form inputs across Registration, Student Enrollment, and Fee Collection feature dark, high-contrast text (`#1E293B`) on solid surfaces with distinct focus highlights for clear legibility."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 171573353
    }
