  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Data Storage Options**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently evaluating the best way to handle multiple accounts and their associated library states. I have Moshi, Room, Kotlin Serialization with Moshi Kotlin, SharedPreferences, and the Android Context at my disposal. The focus is on clean architecture, so I\'m investigating how Moshi, Gson, JSONObject, or SharedPreferences can best facilitate this multi-account storage.\n\n\n**Defining Account Structure**\n\nNow I\'m creating the data structure for account details. I\'m thinking of an `AccountData` class or a `SavedAccount` container. This will include profiles, library details, branches, active branch IDs, SaaS subscriptions, shifts, plans, seats, students, attendance, payments, expenses, registration requests, and audit logs. I\'m focusing on defining the complete set of attributes that must be saved for each account.\n\nI\'m starting to think about handling the initial demo account and new user registrations.\n\n\n**Constructing New Library Workflow**\n\nI\'m now outlining the steps for a new library registration. Upon registration, a pristine workspace will be established, initialized with empty lists for students, attendance, payments, and other transactional details. A single primary branch is generated, and seats are populated as `AVAILABLE`. Shifts are assigned according to the user\'s input, standard pricing plans will be generated, and an audit log entry confirms the successful registration. This also starts the library on a free subscription.\n\n\n**Implementing Login and Persistence**\n\nNow I\'m creating the user login flow, making sure to handle both new and existing accounts. For new users, I\'ll be saving the clean workspace to local storage using the account identifier (user ID, phone, or email). When users log in, the repository will check local storage and restore their exact account data if there\'s a match. I\'ll also add a toast message to confirm their return. If the credentials are wrong, I\'ll provide an informative error message. I\'ll also be implementing autosaving so that every action (student additions/updates, fee collection, attendance marking, seat assignments, etc.) triggers an update to the active account data in the local store.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 423306784
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
