    thinking: "**Considering Storage Options**\n\nOkay, I\'m exploring persistence strategies for accounts. I\'m currently leaning towards `LibraryStorage` or `AccountStore` as potential abstractions. I\'m also considering storing accounts in Android\'s `SharedPreferences` or JSON files within internal app storage, with the option of using Moshi, Org.json, Gson or Room.\n\n\n**Defining Account Data Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'ve defined the data structure for a `SavedLibraryAccount`, which includes fields for ID, owner profile, library details, branches, and various associated data like shifts, payments, and audit logs. I\'m now examining the `LibraryRepository`\'s initialization process. I\'m reviewing how it handles account persistence checks and demo account initialization, alongside initial login states. I\'ll need to figure out how to correctly persist the new user account during registration.\n\n\n**Constructing Registration Logic**\n\nI\'m now deep in the registration flow for new libraries and owner accounts. I\'m focusing on crafting the data required when a new library registers, be it through the `registerFullLibrary` or `registerOwner` functions. The process now encompasses creating an owner profile, setting up a library instance with its main branch, generating available seats, and initializing lists for students, attendance, payments, expenses, registration requests, shifts, and audit logs. I\'m ensuring everything is set up correctly, from SaaS subscriptions to audit trails.\n\n\n**Implementing Persistence Updates**\n\nOkay, I\'ve implemented the crucial part: saving the new account to persistent storage, ensuring everything is freshly initialized and with `_isLoggedIn.value` set to true. I\'ve integrated automatic saving of in-memory data changes for students, payments, expenses, and so on. Now, I\'m focusing on the login mechanisms. The plan is to look up accounts by normalized phone or email, and I\'ll load all existing data upon successful login, setting `_isLoggedIn.value = true`, and I will return true or provide the user with a specific error message.\n\n\n**Finalizing Login Flow**\n\nOkay, I\'m setting the login flow to handle clearing input fields and error messages in `LoginScreen.kt`. I\'m integrating a \"Demo Login\" button to pre-fill test credentials. I\'m ensuring proper error messaging for login failures and a clean slate for all fields in register mode.\n\n\n"
