    thinking: "**Considering Application Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'m thinking about the application structure. I\'m leaning toward a class like `com.example.LibraryApp`, declared in the manifest. This could hold the `applicationContext`, making storage accessible throughout the app in a controlled manner! I think it will be clean and safe!\n\n\n**Designing Account Storage**\n\nI\'ve been designing the `AccountStore`, specifically `LibraryAccountStorage`.  I\'ve detailed two account types: a default demo account with prepopulated sample data, and new registered accounts with clean data.  The demo account is meant to provide a quick start, and a positive user experience.\n\n\n**Initializing Library Data**\n\nRight now, I\'m focusing on the initial data setup. I\'m imagining starting with empty lists for students, attendance, payments, expenses, and registration requests. I\'m also planning to create a set of seats based on capacity, all available initially, with no assigned students or mock data. I\'m thinking of setting up one primary branch, configured shifts, and generated pricing plans, with an initial audit log entry for workspace initialization. The initial SaaS subscription will be the free plan. This will all be persisted under an account key. This new account will then be set as active and logged in.\n\n\n**Implementing Authentication Persistence**\n\nI\'m now implementing the login and persistence flow. On successful authentication, I\'ll verify the password or OTP, then load all the saved fields for the account. These fields are: ownerProfile, library, branches, activeBranchId, saasSubscription, shifts, libraryPlans, seats, students, attendance, payments, expenses, registrationRequests, and auditLogs. Then, I\'ll set the active account, set isLoggedIn to true, and return AuthResult.Success. I am making sure data persistence is continuous and reliable.\n\n\n\n**Defining Account Models**\n\nI\'m now defining the structure of `SavedLibraryAccount`, specifying the models for storing user and library data. I\'ve detailed `OwnerProfile`, `Library`, `Branch`, `SaaSSubscription`, `Shift`, `LibraryPlan`, `Seat`, `Student`, `AttendanceRecord`, `StudentPayment`, `Expense`, `RegistrationRequest`, and `AuditLog`, ensuring everything needed for the app is accounted for!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
